course: dictionary
lesson: 8765
title: Severe: serious, strict or plain
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Severe is a word with three meanings. Most often it means very bad, serious or harmful. «Some people have a severe allergy to stings that can make their throat swell.» A severe allergy is a serious one, so it needs help at once.
explain: Use the clues around the word to choose the right meaning. «When a severe weather warning comes on the radio, listen and do what it says.» The warning tells you the weather could be dangerous, so severe means serious and dangerous here. Check by swapping in another word: serious weather warning still makes sense.
explain: Severe can also mean very strict and harsh, as with a severe teacher in a story who never smiles. It can mean very plain, with no decoration, as with a severe grey dress. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Severe means very bad, serious or harmful.
fact: Severe can describe weather, pain, an allergy or a punishment.
fact: Severe can also mean very strict and harsh, as in a severe teacher.
fact: Severe can also mean very plain, with no decoration.
fact: Severe has the forms more severe and most severe, and also severer and severest.
exercise: «Some people have a severe allergy to stings.» What does severe mean here? | Very small | *Very serious and harmful | Gentle and kind | Very funny
exercise: «When a severe weather warning comes on the radio, listen and do what it says.» What should you do? | Turn the radio off and go to sleep | Ask for a bigger radio | *Listen and follow the advice | Go outside to see the storm
exercise: The story says the teacher was severe. He never smiled and gave hard punishments. What does severe mean? | Very new | *Very strict and harsh | Very cheerful | Very tiny
test: Which phrase from the lessons is about health? | severe punishment | severe weather | severe warning | *severe pain
test: A grey dress has no bows, lace or frills. Which meaning of severe fits it? | Very strict and harsh | Very bad or harmful | *Very plain, with no decoration | Very shiny
exam: Which meaning of severe fits «the judge's severe face, with no smile at all»? | Very quiet | Very plain, with no decoration | *Very strict and harsh | Very bad or harmful
